            "onNodeClick": [
              {
                "type": "script",
                "scope": "G",
                "config": {
                  "script": "\t\t\tsops = {\n\t1: \"Confirm the stop is real: check the HMI banner and the andon. Note the time - the downtime clock starts now. Do not restart anything yet.\",\n\t2: \"Open the alarm summary. An active or recently cleared alarm usually names the root cause directly. If several alarms fired, work the FIRST one chronologically.\",\n\t3: \"Follow the response sheet for that alarm code. If the sheet does not resolve it in 10 minutes, escalate to maintenance and log the code.\",\n\t4: \"Check infeed and outfeed: bottles, caps, labels, glue, CO2. Starvation and blockage look identical to a breakdown from the HMI.\",\n\t5: \"Refill from the buffer or call intralogistics on ext. 4410. Log the starvation as a logistics stop, not an equipment fault.\",\n\t6: \"Inspect guides, star wheels and conveyor transfers for a visible jam. Use the flashlight, not your hands.\",\n\t7: \"LOCK-OUT / TAG-OUT before reaching into the machine. Clear the jam, check for damaged product upstream, remove debris, close guards.\",\n\t8: \"Raise a work order with photos. The on-call escalation order is maintained in Admin > Rosters. Stay with the machine until maintenance arrives.\",\n\t9: \"Ramp up stepwise and watch the first 15 minutes. If the same stop recurs, do NOT keep clearing it - go back into triage and escalate.\",\n\t10: \"Close the stop with an accurate reason code. The weekly Pareto in the morning meeting is built from these codes.\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tself.view.custom.sopTitle = event.name\n\t\t\tself.view.custom.sopBody = sops.get(event.id, 'No SOP on file for this step.')\n"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
